{"ev": "session_end", "final": "I have successfully found and fixed the bug in `stats.py`. \n\n**Cause of the bug:**\nIn the `median` function for even-length lists, the code calculated the average of `s[mid]` and `s[mid + 1]` instead of `s[mid - 1]` and `s[mid]`. For `[1, 2, 3, 4]`, `n = 4`, `mid = 2`, it averaged `s[2]` (3) and `s[3]` (4) resulting in `3.5` instead of averaging `s[1]` (2) and `s[2]` (3) resulting in `2.5`.\n\n**Fix:**\nUpdated `median` to use `(s[mid - 1] + s[mid]) / 2` when `n % 2 == 0`. All tests now pass succes", "steps": 6, "t": 8682584527666, "agent_pid": 35774}
